  "scope": "Complete functional Pater constituent in offered source order: FIDES page-file 0275 (printed p.213), right column from Orémus after the earlier Canon/Iungit manus, through the introduction and adjacent Extendit manus; all page-file 0276 (printed p.214) body text, including the first complete Pater and response/Amen, the governing alternative-cantus rubric for three-lesson feasts, ferial days and Masses for the dead, the separately printed Per omnia/Amen and second introduction/Pater; and page-file 0277 (printed p.215), left column through Sacerdos submissâ voce dicit / Amén. It stops before the right-column Deinde accipit Patenam and Libera nos. Both complete printed chant forms and all governing rubrics are included. Final Amén. preserves the independently preferred probable printed acute over e in a worn/folded area; the hooked mark meets a crease, so that diacritic retains an explicit source-condition reservation. This complete declared functional constituent has partial whole-book and partial post-Canon text coverage. The wider continuation through page-file 0285 remains blocked by concealed source letters and punctuation; no alternate-setting words fill those gaps.",
